  "preamble": "The voiced postalveolar fricative [ʒ] is strengthened to the affricate [dʒ]. It typically happens when a language lacking /ʒ/, or having it only marginally, borrows words with [ʒ]: many English speakers replace the word-final [ʒ] of French loans such as garage and beige with native [dʒ], and Italian, which has no /ʒ/, renders French [ʒ] as [dʒ] in loans such as gilè and bigiotteria.",
